          "prompt": "Stylized hand-painted 3D game environment art for a fast first-person roguelite shooter, matching the\nreadable visual direction of Gunfire Reborn: bold chunky silhouettes, broad clean faceted planes, two or three dominant\ncolour blocks, soft painted gradients and a few restrained edge accents. East-Asian desert temple fantasy. Matte stone,\nwood and cloth, restrained highlights on metal, sparse painted wear. No photorealism, micro-grain, dense tiny cracks,\nelaborate miniature carvings, harsh specular highlights or baked cast shadows. Even neutral lighting.\n\nAsset (4m wide x 3m tall x 4m deep): A square raised temple podium module 4m wide, 3m tall, 4m deep for tiling into large terraces: solid sandstone block walls with a carved horizontal frieze band, a projecting cap moulding and a flat paved top. Warm ochre stone, faded teal and gold frieze accents. All four sides finished identically so modules tile edge to edge.\n\nOutput: one orthographic model turnaround sheet for 3D reconstruction. Exactly four separate complete views\nof the SAME object in one row, left to right: FRONT view, LEFT side view, BACK view, RIGHT side view. Same scale and same\nground line in all four, each centred in its quarter with generous empty margin, never touching or overlapping.\nPlain flat light neutral grey background (#D6D6D6). No floor, no ground shadow, no text, no labels, no frames, no\nperspective.",
